Expected elements: present

Identity bar (exit `← aztec`, `0xb63616…6359`, `Partial`, `block 101`, eight stepping buttons in both directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, phase rail) present; `CODE` positioned at line 32; `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` as one tab strip with Call Trace open and seven frames; `VALUES` a separate pane below with eleven rows; `TRANSACTION` carrying `DATA` + `Synthetic demo data` + the producer's sentences. No band above the bar, no spinner, no empty pane.

Removing the band was right, but the ~190 px came back as slack rather than as information. The middle column is now 47% empty: the Call Trace region holds 604 px and its content stops at y≈320, leaving ~348 px of blank pane under `By call order · Self cost`, while the Values pane ends 130 px short of its own floor and the Transaction pane beside it is cut mid-JSON at the viewport edge. The Code pane took its share as eight more rows at a 23 px pitch on 13 px type instead of a tighter listing.

Small text mostly holds (line numbers 5.5:1, prose 5.8:1), with two exceptions: the iteration chips run 3.3–3.5:1, and the provenance paragraph — the pane's most important claim — is set right-aligned, nine ragged-left lines, unlike every other paragraph in that pane.

Fixes: give the Values pane the call trace's dead height; left-align the `DATA` prose.

Rating: 6/10

